  {
   "uuid": "ae2e554b-b4d9-4fe3-ad7c-f592e9f59ae1",
   "text": "",
   "content": [
    {
     "start_timestamp": "2026-07-16T02:30:02.000000Z",
     "stop_timestamp": "2026-07-16T02:30:12.629000Z",
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Almost certainly a scam. Several classic signs at once:\n\n- **Price**: a 1BR in the Inner Sunset well below typical market rent.\n- **Owner abroad, can't show it**: the most common rental scam story.\n- **Keys mailed after payment**: you'd pay before seeing the place or meeting anyone.\n- **Zelle**: no buyer protection; once sent, the money is gone.\n\nRules that rule out most scams:\n- Never pay before seeing the unit in person (or via a live video walkthrough where *you* direct the camera, plus confirming the person has access).\n- Reverse-image-search the photos; scam listings often reuse photos from real listings.\n- Look up the address and owner in public records if possible.\n- Pay deposits by check or a traceable method, against a written lease.",
     "citations": []
    }
   ],
   "sender": "assistant",
   "index": 1,
